"""navera_lite/ros/arbiter_v0.py — arbiter v0, NAVERA Lite's first judge: NAIVE ON PURPOSE. Part of NAVERA
Lite, the course's teaching stack (given in mission 09; you attack it from outside in 10 and fix its holes in 12;
mission 29 replaces it).
Written for the course; it is not NAVERA code.

    python3 -m navera_lite.ros.arbiter_v0 --ros-args --params-file navera_lite.yaml
    python3 -m navera_lite.ros.arbiter_v0 --ros-args --params-file navera_lite.yaml -p use_eligible:=true

Its rules (and their holes, which mission 12 makes you find):
  - priority GPS > day > night > celestial (estimate.SOURCES): the first usable source wins;
  - usable = valid, a finite position, not older than the source's timeout. A stamp from the future is
    never "old", so v0 takes it (hole);
  - GPS fixes go through the jump gate of mission 01 (guard.JumpGate) before they are stored;
  - FIX if σ = √max(a, c) ≤ fix_max_sigma_m, else DEGRADED. v0 reads σ from the numbers without asking
    whether they ARE a covariance or whether the type says they mean anything (holes);
  - STARTING before the first position, NO_FIX when no source is usable (the reason lists why).
With use_eligible:=true (from mission 12) it asks YOUR estimate.eligible() and estimate.stated_sigma()
instead of its naive tests, and the attacks of mission 12 stop working.

Topics (names are relative: a namespace moves them, e.g. /drone/navera_lite/fix/gps):
  subscribes  navera_lite/fix/{gps,day,night,celestial}  NavSatFix (FIX_QOS)
              navera_lite/imu                            Imu (SENSOR_QOS), liveness only
  publishes   navera_lite/position  NavSatFix, the winning measurement, once per new measurement (FIX_QOS)
              navera_lite/status    DiagnosticStatus, on every arrival and at tick_hz (STATUS_QOS, latched)
"""
import math

from diagnostic_msgs.msg import DiagnosticStatus
from rclpy.node import Node
from sensor_msgs.msg import Imu, NavSatFix

from navera_lite import estimate
from navera_lite.estimate import SOURCES, TIMEOUT_KEY, classify, horizontal
from navera_lite.geo import is_finite_latlon
from navera_lite.guard import JumpGate
from navera_lite.ros.convert import from_navsatfix, make_status, to_navsatfix
